.TH MC1-FW-ZONE-GUARD 8 "2026-10-28" "mu2edaq-batch-queues" "Mu2e DAQ Tools"
.SH NAME
mc1-fw-zone-guard \- keep the MC1 Slurm firewalld zone file in place
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mc1-fw-zone-guard
.RB [ \-z
.IR zone ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR store ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR zonedir ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ sync | check | save | restore ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Slurm traffic between MC1 cluster members is accepted by the firewalld zone
.B 10_mc1_cluster
(design decision D16). If its file
.I /etc/firewalld/zones/10_mc1_cluster.xml
disappears, cluster traffic falls into the site zone
.B 50_FNAL
(target REJECT). slurmd can then no longer reach slurmctld, and every
compute node goes
.BR down* .
This happened on all nodes during site maintenance on 2026-10-16.
.PP
.B mc1-fw-zone-guard
keeps a copy of the live zone file in a store outside
.I /etc/firewalld
and puts the file back when it is missing (D24). The copy is always taken from
the live file, so it follows changes that Ansible roles make to the zone.
.PP
The firewall role installs it as
.I /usr/local/sbin/mc1-fw-zone-guard
with the units
.B mc1-fw-zone-guard.service
(oneshot; runs when firewalld starts and at boot, ordered before slurmd and
slurmctld) and
.B mc1-fw-zone-guard.timer
(every
.BR mc1_fw_guard_interval ,
default 5 min).
.SH MODES
.TP
.B sync
Default. If the live file is present, refresh the saved copy when it differs,
and reload firewalld if the running firewall lacks the zone. If the live file
is missing, install the saved copy, run
.BR restorecon (8)
on it, then
.BR "firewall-cmd \-\-reload" .
.TP
.B check
Report only. Exits 0 when the live file is present, the saved copy matches it,
and the running firewall has the zone; otherwise exits 1 and names what is
wrong.
.B mc1-slurm-deploy validate
records this as
.BR fw_zone_guard .
.TP
.B save
Copy the live file to the store.
.TP
.B restore
Install the saved copy and reload, even if a live file exists.
.SH OPTIONS
Options override the environment, which overrides
.IR /etc/sysconfig/mc1-fw-zone-guard ,
which overrides the defaults.
.TP
.BI \-z " zone"
Zone name. Env
.BR MC1_FW_ZONE ;
default
.BR 10_mc1_cluster .
.TP
.BI \-s " store"
Directory for the saved copy (created 0700). Env
.BR MC1_FW_GUARD_STORE ;
default
.IR /var/lib/mc1-slurm/firewalld .
.TP
.BI \-d " zonedir"
firewalld permanent zone directory. Env
.BR MC1_FW_ZONE_DIR ;
default
.IR /etc/firewalld/zones .
.TP
.B \-n
Dry run: print what would change and change nothing.
.TP
.B \-q
Print only changes and problems.
.TP
.B \-h
Usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Nothing to do, or the action succeeded.
.TP
1
.BR check :
something is missing or stale. Other modes: a copy, install or reload failed.
.TP
2
The live file is missing and there is no saved copy. Re-run the firewall role.
.TP
64
Usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/mc1-slurm/firewalld/10_mc1_cluster.xml
Saved copy.
.TP
.I /etc/sysconfig/mc1-fw-zone-guard
Settings read by the systemd unit.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/mc1-fw-zone-guard.{service,timer}
Units.
.SH EXAMPLES
State of one node:
.PP
.EX
mc1-fw-zone-guard check
journalctl -t mc1-fw-zone-guard
systemctl list-timers mc1-fw-zone-guard.timer
.EE
.PP
State of every node from the operator machine:
.PP
.EX
ansible slurm_cluster -i config/inventory.yml -a 'mc1-fw-zone-guard check' < /dev/null > fw-check.txt
.EE
.PP
Preview a restore without changing anything:
.PP
.EX
mc1-fw-zone-guard \-n sync
.EE
.SH NOTES
The guard repairs a deletion; it cannot prevent one. A restore that happens
while the node is up leaves a gap of up to one timer period. If slurmd was
started during such a gap, its configless start may time out; restart it with
.BR "systemctl restart slurmd" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc1-slurm-deploy (1),
.BR firewall-cmd (1),
.BR firewalld.zone (5),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
